.\" Manual page for arjax
.TH ARJAX 1 "August 2026" "Arjax 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
arjax \- Universal cross-distribution package helper and manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arjax
.br
.B arjax
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBarjax\fR is a unified, provider-agnostic package manager wrapper designed to search, install, upgrade, and manage software across native distribution package managers (pacman, apt, dnf, zypper), AUR, Flatpak, Snap, GitHub releases, and vendor scripts.

Invoking \fBarjax\fR with no arguments in the CLI launches the interactive Terminal User Interface (TUI) by default.

It provides an interactive Ratatui-like TUI, parallel multi-package downloads with progress bars, DAG-based orphan detection, transaction history & rollback, system health diagnostics, and declarative recipe auto-syncing.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
\fBsearch\fR \fIQUERY\fR
Search for software across all enabled providers concurrently.

.TP
\fBinstall\fR \fIPACKAGE...\fR [\fB--provider\fR, \fB-p\fR \fIPROVIDER\fR]
Install one or multiple packages concurrently. Supports parallel multi-package installation with progress meters, provider hints, and automatic fallback suggestions on failure.

.TP
\fBremove\fR \fIPACKAGE\fR
Uninstall a package using the appropriate provider.

.TP
\fBupdate\fR, \fBupgrade\fR
Check for and apply system software updates across distribution repositories and flatpaks.

.TP
\fBtui\fR
Launch the interactive Terminal User Interface featuring live search, package browser, dependency tree visualization, transaction log inspector, orphan scanner, and system health dashboard.

.TP
\fBrecipes\fR [\fBlist\fR | \fBsync\fR | \fBupdate\fR]
Manage declarative software recipes.
.RS
.IP \fBlist\fR
Display available local recipes, remote versions, and update status.
.IP \fBsync\fR, \fBupdate\fR
Auto-pull recipe updates from upstream central registry into ~/.config/arjax/recipes/.
.RE

.TP
\fBhistory\fR [\fBlist\fR | \fBrollback\fR \fITX_ID\fR]
Inspect and manage package transaction logs.
.RS
.IP \fBlist\fR
List recorded installation and removal operations with timestamps and status.
.IP \fBrollback\fR \fITX_ID\fR
Rollback a specific past transaction (reversing installs into removals and removals into installs).
.RE

.TP
\fBcleanup orphans\fR [\fB--dry-run\fR]
Scan for unused orphan packages using Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) dependency analysis.

.TP
\fBstats\fR
Display interactive System Statistics & Health Diagnostics Dashboard (disk usage, package counts, pending updates, orphan count, systemd health alerts).

.TP
\fBcompletion\fR [\fBshow\fR | \fBinstall\fR] \fISHELL\fR
Generate or install shell autocompletions for \fIbash\fR, \fIzsh\fR, or \fIfish\fR.

.TP
\fBsetup\fR [\fB--mode\fR \fInormal|advanced\fR]
Interactive onboarding setup for profile configuration and background update monitoring.

.SH TUI KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Enter
Install selected package
.TP
.B d
Show Dependency Tree Visualization
.TP
.B h
Inspect Transaction History Log
.TP
.B o
Scan for Orphan Packages (DAG analysis)
.TP
.B s
Display System Statistics & Health Diagnostics Dashboard
.TP
.B u
Sync Declarative Recipes from central registry
.TP
.B q
Quit TUI

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/arjax/config.json
User configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/arjax/history.json
Transaction log history storage.
.TP
.I ~/.arjax/logs/arjax.log
Detailed application execution and error logs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/arjax/recipes/
Custom and auto-synced declarative package recipes.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR apt (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR snap (1)

